es-rgds-screensaver-controls: touch controls on the bottom panel during the screensaver

With es-rgds-screensaver.patch the screensaver runs on the top panel and the bottom one stays black, its backlight
off (dii-ess-aye/device/screensaver-panel.sh). A tap on the bottom panel now shows controls there for 10 s:

- the status: Wi-Fi (connected, not connected, off) and the battery (level, charging), in the status bar's colours
  when COLOURED STATUS ICONS is on (es-rgds-battery-charging.patch; plain without it);
- the slide's game, with NEXT SLIDE and PLAY THIS GAME (ES's slideshow is random and keeps no history, so there is no
  previous slide);
- the music: the song, NEXT SONG and STOP MUSIC (PLAY MUSIC when none plays), or "Music is off".

Each tap keeps them up for another 10 s; a tap on the top panel or any button closes the screensaver as before. They
are drawn in the theme's menu colours and font, sized against the 480 px panel of the RG DS.

Window::processMouseButton offers the tap to the screensaver first, through a new ScreenSaver::onMouseClick (the
default takes nothing, so other screensavers are unchanged): the bottom panel's taps are taken, the press acts and its
release is swallowed. The screensaver fires a new event, screensaver-controls show/hide, and screensaver-panel.sh
lights the backlight it turned off while they show. While they show, getNextUpdateTimeout wakes each second, for the
status and the song, and when they close; fades still draw every frame. One-panel layouts have no bottom panel and
no controls.

